From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:46:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: the computer name without wineboot (patch 0486)

Unrailed 2: Back on Track stopped at its start on the console:
GetComputerNameW failed with ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND. The NetBIOS name is
read from ActiveComputerName, a volatile key wineboot writes at each
start, and wineboot never runs in a title.

Patch 0486: when the key is missing, GetComputerNameExW reads the
configured name the prefix keeps, as wineboot would have copied it.

Tested on the PC's Wine, 64- and 32-bit: with ActiveComputerName
deleted, GetComputerNameW and GetComputerNameExW(ComputerNameNetBIOS)
return the prefix's name.
